KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11 --unwind 5 --no-unwinding-assertions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
std::tuple basic operations in C++11 mode.

This test passed only vacuously until the parameter-pack-arity fix: the tuple
elements are compile-time constants, so std::get<0> of t == 1 and std::get<1>
of t == 2 were folded to true and the assertions removed before symbolic
execution -- std::get was never exercised at run time.

Resolving a directly-deduced type-internal parameter pack to its full arity
during the deferred method-body drain -- the fix this accompanies -- makes the
std::get calls genuine run-time calls.  The run-time std::get chain
std::get -> std::__get_helper -> std::_Tuple_impl::_M_head ->
std::_Head_base::_M_head is not fully instantiated for the tail elements, so
std::get<1> of t returns a nondet value and its assertion fails: VERIFICATION
FAILED.

This is a known bug in the run-time std::get chain instantiation, a separate
layer from the pack-arity fix.  Flip back to CORE once that chain instantiates
correctly so the assertions are verified non-vacuously.
